 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-4290 with Advisor/Governor/Phase/Registry/
  Store/Operation/Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-4329/4390 module-for-
  module, adapted from building-installation-trade hazards to other-civil-
  engineering excavation/buried-utility hazards -- civilworks.* namespace,
  Civil Works Governor):
  - Governor: eight concrete HARD checks (unknown-op / effect-not-propose /
    forbidden-action-class / site-not-verified / no-legal-basis / utility-
    survey-incomplete / excavation-shoring-noncompliant / unresolved-
    safety-concern), all un-overridable by human approval, plus a
    confidence/high-stakes escalation gate (SOFT, human may approve)
  - Facts: per-jurisdiction legal-basis catalog (JPN/USA/DEU seeded) with
    two independent real legal bases each -- :utility-survey-basis
    (pre-work buried-utility/ground-condition investigation duty) and
    :excavation-shoring-basis (trench/excavation-collapse protection duty).
    JPN (labor safety and health ordinance Art.355 pre-work survey /
    Art.356 slope-gradient table, 2.0m quantitative trigger for the
    ordinary-ground row) and USA (OSHA 29 CFR 1926.651(b) utility-location
    duty / 1926.652 protective-system duty, 1.5m/5ft quantitative trigger)
    are :quantitative; DEU/EU (SS16 DGUV Vorschrift 38/39 utility-inquiry
    duty / DGUV Regel 101-604 + DIN 4124 soil-classification-dependent
    shoring duty) is honestly :qualitative -- no fabricated numeric
    trigger.
  - Registry: pure functions -- site-record-log/schedule-proposal/safety-
    concern-flag/supply-order-proposal jurisdiction-scoped sequence-numbered
    record construction, safety-concern-notice document rendering citing
    the jurisdiction's legal basis inline
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (default, atom-backed) + DatomicStore
    (langchain.db + langchain-store.core field-spec/identity-schema/
    event-log helpers per ADR-2607141600) -- both pass the same contract
    test, 8-site seed set covering happy path + every failure mode +
    cross-jurisdiction + qualitative-jurisdiction scenarios
  - Advisor: CivilWorksAdvisor -- deterministic mock (default) + llm-advisor
    (langchain.model-backed, same proposal-EDN contract)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate, :flag-safety-concern permanently absent from
    every phase's :auto set (structural, not a milestone); :log-site-record/
    :schedule-construction-operation/:order-supplies MAY auto-commit at
    phase 3 when governor-clean and confident
  - Operation: OperationActor -- full langgraph-clj StateGraph (advise ->
    govern -> decide -> commit|hold|request-approval), real
    interrupt-before/resume approval workflow, safety-concern notice
    (mail+phone via caller-injected fn-notifier, no JVM interop) sent only
    after human approval
  - Sim: demo runner (-main) exercising all four happy paths across JPN/
    USA/DEU + all six HARD-hold scenarios directly
  - Ops (closed allowlist, all :effect :propose): log-site-record
    (progress/material-usage/utility-survey data logging), schedule-
    construction-operation (industrial-plant/pipeline/power-line/outdoor-
    sports-facility scheduling proposal), flag-safety-concern (buried-
    utility-strike/excavation-collapse/structural concern -- ALWAYS
    escalates), order-supplies (materials/equipment procurement proposal)
  - Tests: 69 tests / 247 assertions across
    facts/governor-contract/notify/phase/registry/store-contract, all green
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop, no new Rust/robot-control code),
    AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - GitHub repo created directly as cloud-itonami-isic-4290 (no rename
    needed)"

